"""Insights: the Product+ articles, published in full on productadvisory.co.

Each article is published here first, then as the Product+ Newsletter issue on LinkedIn (with "Originally published
at productadvisory.co/insights/<slug>" at the end). Articles without a "body" yet are listed on the Insights page and
link to LinkedIn until their full text is added.

A body is a list of blocks:
    ("p", "text")                     a paragraph (inline HTML allowed: <b>, <i>, <a>)
    ("h2", "heading")                 a section heading; the section that follows is searchable by Ask
    ("h3", "heading")
    ("ul", ["item", ...])  ("ol", ["item", ...])
    ("quote", "text")                 a pulled quote
    ("fig", "file.webp", "alt text", "caption or empty")   an image from assets/insights/<slug>/
"takeaways" (a short list shown first, "Key takeaways") and "faq" (question and answer pairs, shown at the end and
marked up as FAQPage) are optional; write them to answer directly, from what the article says. "updated" (a date) is
optional and becomes dateModified. "draft": True builds the page as a hidden preview (marked noindex) but lists it
nowhere: not on the Insights or home page, in the sitemap, Ask or Related reading. Remove it to publish. "linkedin" is
optional until the article is on LinkedIn.
"services" lists the related services (ids in content.SERVICES): the article ends with them, and each service on
the Services page lists the articles that name it under "Related reading".
Images: assets/insights/<slug>/cover.webp (1600x900), card.webp (800x450, the index card) and og.jpg (1200x675,
the sharing image)."""

# The three subjects the Insights page filters by, each with its own colour (--cat-<id> in site.css) wherever an
