            ("p", "Weighted scoring starts with a decision about what matters. You choose a handful of criteria, give each one a weight, and score every option on each criterion, usually from 1 to 5. Costs such as effort and risk count the other way round, so lower is better. Each option's weighted total becomes its score."),
